WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Jesus taught his followers
to love their enemies.

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.370
Many early Christian writers
opposed Christians fighting at all.

3
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:12.110
Yet in the 5th century, Augustine of
Hippo argued that war could sometimes be

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.650
a duty, to restore peace.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.670
Today, the Geneva Conventions
limit how armies may fight.

6
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.070
So can a war ever be just?

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.660
And who sets the rules for fighting one?

8
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.890
In this mission, you'll
read Augustine and Aquinas,

9
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.900
and raise the three pillars
Aquinas said a just war needs.

10
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.060
Then you'll trace how the theory grew
from church teaching into international

11
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:35.990
law.

12
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.680
Your mission: find out whether
a war can ever be just,

13
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.870
and who sets the rules for fighting one.
